{"availability":"available","full":"OSS-Initiatives-IIIT-Sonepat/vlabs-iiit-sonepat","name":"vlabs-iiit-sonepat","description":"The Virtual Labs Project — a student-led, open-source, non-profit initiative presenting ECE and Electronics laboratory experiments through interactive 3D environments.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":8,"forks":13,"created":"2026-08-06T12:43:40Z","updated":"2026-10-06T16:46:53Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://vlabs-iiit-sonepat.vercel.app","topics":["ece","electronics-engineering","electronics-lab","threejs"],"demo":"https://vlabs-iiit-sonepat.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T17:55:02.170Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T17:55:02.170Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T17:55:02.170Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T17:55:02.170Z","stars":8,"forks":13}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Interactive 3D virtual ECE laboratories. In your browser. Free to use. Libre and open source. Built as a non-profit, student-led initiative.","VLabs is a browser-based platform that recreates real electronics lab sessions as interactive 3D experiences. Students can place components on a virtual breadboard, wire them step by step, read theory, run simulations, and follow the full aim → theory → apparatus → procedure → observations → conclusion flow — all without touching any hardware.","Every 3D component — breadboard, resistor, LED, IC, capacitor, wire — is built from raw Three.js geometry. No GLTF models. No black-box 3D engines. Every pin, copper strip, and colour band is procedurally generated code you can read and understand."],"features":["Analog electronics (rectifiers, diodes, Thevenin, Norton, Kirchhoff)","Digital electronics (logic gates, adders, multiplexers, flip-flops, counters)","Combinational arithmetic (CLA adder, Booth's multiplier, Wallace tree)","Memory & CPU systems (ALU simulation, cache models, CPU design)","8085 assem